        <groundspeak:log id="346811596">
          <groundspeak:log_wpt lat="53.374600" lon="-117.716167" />
          <groundspeak:date>2013-09-01T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1074559">van der Decken</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP596 - Old Entrance

Elev. 1047 metres&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Before starting the long, long drive back home I made one last drive west for this cap. In a continuing theme in Alberta this summer, the bridge across the river was under construction and was down to a single lane. All I've got to say (all that's printable, in any case) about the timing on the lights is that's the [i]longest[/i] three minutes I've ever sat through in my life! Once that was over it was up the hill and left onto the Brule Road. I'd no sooner made the turn off the highway when I spotted PDOP's trail head up ahead at the corner. There was no problem pulling off to the side to park (it'd likely be a very different story in winter) near the trailhead. A short walk up a sandy hill and I spotted another trail heading off in a direction that paralleled the road. I followed that to an animal trail that took me out to the hillside no more than 20 metres from the cap.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The cap is well above ground and in excellent shape. It sits a bit behind the marker post and shouldn't be any problem to find even in deep snow. You also get a great panoramic view overlooking the highway.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the cap, outforthehunt.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Trailhead: N53 22.411 W117 42.694

Junction: N53 22.385 W117 42.758

Animal trail: N53 22.429 W117 42.977&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
      </groundspeak:logs>
